==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|vika|vīka}}, from {{inh|sv|non|[[víkja]], [[víkva]]|tr=to fold, turn, head in a direction}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*wīkwaną}}. Cognate to {{cog|sv|vicka|tr=wiggle}}.

The adverb in the phrase ''ge vika'' comes from Low German ''wike/weke gewen'', where the noun ''wike'' means ''concession, escape''.<ref>{{R:runeberg.org|saol|6|0303.html Vika}}</ref> Compare German {{m|sv|weichen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|sv|Sv-vika.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-irr|viker|vek|[[vikt]] or [[vikit]]|vik}}

# to [[fold]] (into several layers)
#: {{ux|sv|De '''vikte''' tvätt|They were '''folding''' laundry}}
# {{lb|sv|colloquial}} to [[dedicate]] (time), to [[designate]] a period of time for a certain action
#: {{ux|sv|Jag '''viker''' en dag åt [[mässa]]n.|I '''am dedicating''' a day to the expo.}}
# {{lb|sv|colloquial}} to dedicate, to set aside for a special person or a special use
#: {{ux|sv|De här kakorna har jag '''vikt''' åt stackars Tom – rör dem inte!|These cookies I have '''put aside''' for poor Tom – don't touch them!}}
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to [[give up]], to [[give in]] (under pressure), to [[budge]]
#: {{ux|sv|Mona Sahlin '''viker sig''' inte i första taget.|{{w|Mona Sahlin}} doesn't '''give up''' easily.}}
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to [[bend]] (for example from laughing or in pain)
#: {{ux|sv|De skrattade så att de '''vek''' sig.|They were rolling on the floor laughing.}}
# {{lb|sv|usually with {{m|sv|in}}}} to [[turn]] (slightly, while moving)
#: {{ux|sv|Vi '''vek in''' på en stig som vi aldrig hade gått förut|We '''turned onto''' a path that we had never walked before}}
# {{lb|sv|with {{m|sv|av}}}} to [[turn]] (while moving (so as to deviate from a path – sometimes figuratively))
#: {{ux|sv|Vi '''vek av''' från huvudleden, in på en grusväg|We '''turned off''' the main road onto a dirt road}}
# {{lb|sv|with {{m|sv|av}}}} to [[deviate]] (more generally)
#: {{syn|sv|avvika|q=more common}}
# {{lb|sv|in "vika åt sidan" or "vika hädan"}} to [[move]] [[aside]], (often) to [[step aside]]
#: {{ux|sv|Folk '''vek åt sidan''' när han gick genom rummet med svärdet i hand|People '''moved aside''' as he walked through the room with his sword in hand}}
#: {{ux|sv|'''Vik hädan''' dödlig!|'''Step aside''', mortal!}}
# {{lb|sv|transitive}} {{q|vika ut}} to [[unfold]], to open a [[foldout]]
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} {{q|vika ut}} to expose oneself as a (more-or-less nude) [[centerfold]], to appear (nude) in a magazine or online
#: {{ux|sv|Ungdomar '''viker ut sig''' som aldrig förr.|Youngsters '''expose themselves''' like never before.}}
# {{lb|sv|reflexive|figuratively}} to [[talk]] [[openly]] (on personal topics)
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to [[sleep]], to go to bed
#: {{ux|sv|Jag går och '''viker mig'''.|I'm going to '''go to bed'''.}}

